# Cryptography policy for .claude/hooks/pqc-check.py (run by the commit gate).
#
# profile nist   FIPS-approved + PQC ready: ML-KEM (FIPS 203), ML-DSA (FIPS 204),
#                SLH-DSA (FIPS 205), AES-GCM, SHA-2/SHA-3, HMAC, PBKDF2, TLS 1.3.
# profile cnsa2  NSA CNSA 2.0 on top: AES-256, SHA-384/512, ML-KEM-1024, ML-DSA-87.
profile nist

# Exceptions, one per line, each with a reason (three words or more):
#   allow <rule|category|*> <path-glob> [until=YYYY-MM-DD] -- <reason>
# A `quantum` exception needs until= on or before 2035-12-31 (NIST IR 8547 draft:
# classical public-key crypto is disallowed after 2035). Expired entries fail the gate,
# and entries that match nothing are reported so they can be removed.
# List the rules with: python3 .claude/hooks/pqc-check.py --list-rules
#
# allow quantum-jwt packages/api/src/api/auth.py until=2030-12-31 -- verifies IdP RS256 tokens; IdP has no ML-DSA yet
